    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d912">

                <pb facs="0973" n="961" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg961"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 P.W./6–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-20T18:00:00+03:00">June 20, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2187. Emb’s 2135, June 17.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d912-f1"/> Supporting our
                    notification to Soviet Govt that Amer Govt was informing Italian Govt it would
                    welcome Italian declaration of war on Japan British Amb<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d912-f2"/> on June 17 wrote Molotov<anchor n="17" xml:id="d912-f3"/>
                    that his Govt agreed with proposed American action. Clark Kerr added that
                    British had reed no communication from Italians on subject and did not intend to
                    raise question with them. <pb facs="0974" n="962" xml:id="pg962"/> British
                    Ambassador Rome<anchor n="18" xml:id="d912-f4"/> instructed to say, if queried
                    by Italians, that British were consulted by Americans and agreed to American
                    proposed action.</p>
                <p>Rptd London 307, Rome 49.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
